  "limits": [
    "Only fixed nonempty loops with an unmodified induction variable, no early exits or nested loops, and a predicate distinguishing the first iteration are selected. The 32-iteration minimum is a profitability threshold.",
    "No processor names, field names, or specific array capacities drive selection. Existing counted-loop recognition, call graph, validation and analyses are reused.",
    "No new memory-independence or writable-reference exclusivity assumption is introduced; all original operations keep their order.",
    "The ordinary processor bank retains its cached-output stores and generated LLVM IR. Routing-state pruning and cached-output liveness remain separate work.",
    "Some direct local-state recurrences remain scalar after peeling; the additional plain-array probe did not improve measurably.",
    "The changed callback cases add approximately 4-6 ms to native JIT compilation in these runs. These are debug compiler measurements.",
    "Timing noise in unchanged controls is not a generated-DSP regression: all six controls have identical LLVM IR. These measurements do not establish performance on every target or source program."
